## 3. SysCap bulk residual (~344 files) — class inventory

**Policy this wave:** inventory only. **Do not** mass-edit 344 files. ProcessCap only if file calls `sys_exec` / `sys_spawn` / `async_spawn_internal` (spawn family).

### Live counts

| Metric | Value |
|--------|------:|
| Files with `&SysCap` string | **344** |
| Files with `name: &SysCap` param | **113** |
| Non-comment param occurrences | **~256** |
| Files with `&ProcessCap` | **0** |
| Total `.oo` in external std | **561** |

### Residual class (a–d)

Classification is **heuristic** (signature + body markers). Honest floors — not a compiler proof.

| Class | Meaning | Files | Share |
|-------|---------|------:|------:|
| **(a) real OS** | Calls hard Sys sealed path that is product-backed or hard-Sys-only (`python_embed*`, prctl/epoll/inotify family) | **1** | 0.3% |
| **(b) process** | Calls spawn/exec family (`async_spawn_internal` / `sys_exec` / `sys_spawn`) — ProcessCap preferred at CAP-G4 | **1** | 0.3% |
| **(c) overbroad pure** | `&SysCap` on pure/types or param without real OS effect / without fail-closed stub body — least-privilege debt | **206** | 59.9% |
| **(d) stub** | Fail-closed residual (`Unimplemented` / `COMPILER LIMITATION` / `process_exit(1)`) with SysCap as default-deny gate | **136** | 39.5% |
| **Total** | | **344** | 100% |

#### (a) real OS — named

| File | Why |
|------|-----|
| `std/python.oo` | `load_model` → `python_embed_internal` — **hard SysCap only** (CAP-G4). Alpha returns Err (no CPython) — still correct hard-Sys class, not ProcessCap. |

#### (b) process — named (ProcessCap candidate this wave? **optional**)

| File | Why | Recommendation |
|------|-----|----------------|
| `std/async.oo` | `spawn_task` → `async_spawn_internal`; `join_task` → `async_join_internal` | **Split residual:** spawn prefers **ProcessCap** (SysCap supersede); **join is hard SysCap-only**. Facade today is still single `&SysCap`. ProcessCap-only migrate of whole file would be dishonest without splitting join. **Not required this turn** per power law. |

**ProcessCap scan result:** **zero** files call `sys_exec` / `sys_spawn` / `spawn_process` in external `std/`. Only `async_spawn_internal` in `async.oo`. Product `ooda/std/os/process.oo` (outside this tree) still SysCap facades — see `cap_g6_syscap_inventory.oot`.

#### (c) overbroad pure — bulk shape

| Sub-bucket | Count | Notes |
|------------|------:|-------|
| Comment-only SysCap (RULES boilerplate on pure/types) | **~173** | e.g. many `*_types.oo` / engine pure files under `src/ooda/{sec,auto,aero,crypto,…}` — **no param**, should eventually drop comment or stay doc-only |
| Param overbroad (has `x: &SysCap`, no stub/hard call) | **~33** | e.g. `crypto/fhe.oo`, `quantum/circuit_sim.oo`, `robot/locomotion.oo`, several `*_types`/`*_engine` — pure math/policy taking SysCap |

**Domain density (c):** `src/ooda/sec` ~100 · `auto` ~20 · `crypto` ~17 · `aero` ~14 · `3d` ~10 · physics/bio/robot/quantum/grid/gui/enterprise remainder.

**Next wave (not this):** strip comment-only SysCap from pure modules; drop params where body is pure; do **not** invent ProcessCap for pure crypto.

#### (d) stub — bulk shape

| Sub-bucket | Count | Notes |
|------------|------:|-------|
| Param + fail-closed stub | **~78** | Domain hardware/OS residual entry points gated by SysCap then `process_exit`/`Err` |
| Comment + stub markers (sibling residual) | **~58** | types/ops files in stub packages |

**Domain density (d):** `src/ooda/sec` ~76 (crypto/sys/net/cps heavy) · aero ~11 · enterprise/auto/gui/3d/grid/bio/quantum/robot/edge/crypto/fin remainder.

**Correctness note:** many stubs **should** keep a capability gate (default-deny). Class (d) is "not product-live", not "delete the cap". Prefer future granular only when a sealed op exists (ProcessCap for exec; hard Sys for prctl/python_embed; residual HW stays CAP-G3 type-only).

